Package: DISCO4HD
Title: Distance of Covariance (DISCO) as a Measure of Homeostatic Dysregulation
Version: 0.3.2
Authors@R:
    person("Meng", "Hao", email = "haombio@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Computation of the Distance of Covariance (DISCO), a correlation-based
    measure of homeostatic dysregulation. DISCO quantifies, for each individual, how much
    the pairwise correlation structure of a set of biomarkers deviates from that of a
    young reference population, weighted by the age-association of each biomarker. The
    package provides the core 'cal_disco()' function (with single-threaded, parallel and
    Rcpp/OpenMP backends) and a block-wise decomposition helper. See Hao et al.
    "Distance of Covariance (DISCO): A Novel Measure of Network Homeostatic
    Dysregulation Reveals Organ System Interconnections Underlying Mortality and Disease
    Risk".
